  "display": {
    "case_id": "112400",
    "target_stage": "Delhi High Court appeal under s. 39 after remand to the Rent Control Tribunal for a finding on reasonably suitable residential accommodation",
    "target_court": "Delhi High Court",
    "records": [
      {
        "source_id": "IK-112400:L123:span1",
        "aliases": {},
        "document_id": "112400",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "The appellant took on lease, the first floor of the premises in question from the respondent on January 22, 1964 on a monthly rent of Rs. 250."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-112400:L124:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-112400:L124:span2": [
            0,
            92
          ],
          "IK-112400:L124:span3": [
            331,
            436
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "112400",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "The respondent who was the owner of the entire premises was then occupying the ground floor. The landlord filed an application, before the Rent Controller on November 26.1964 for eviction of the appellant from the portion in his occupation as lessee, on two grounds; (a) that the tenant has sub-let a part of the premises, and (b) that he required the premises bona fide for his occupation as a residence himself and his family members. The latter claim was based under cl."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-112400:L127:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-112400:L127:span4": [
            107,
            193
          ],
          "IK-112400:L127:span5": [
            381,
            481
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "112400",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "The tenant opposed the claim of the landlord on both the grounds. He denied the allegation of sub-letting. He also contended that the landlord's requirement for his occupation was not bonafide. The tenant's plea was that the portion of the premises in his occupation was sufficient for his purpose. The Rent Controller accepted the plea of the tenant that there was no subletting. He also accepted his plea that the requirement of the landlord for his occupation was not bona fide."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-112400:L130:span6",
        "aliases": {},
        "document_id": "112400",
        "stage": "PRIOR_COURT_FINDING",
        "text": "It is the view of both the Tribunals that when eviction is asked for within about I I months of the letting, the claim of the landlord cannot be considered to be bonafide."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-112400:L137:context-v4",
        "aliases": {},
        "document_id": "112400",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "Before the High Court, counsel for both parties made a representation that the Rent Control Tribunal has not recorded a finding on the question whether the premises avaiable with the landlord can be considered to be \"reasonably suitable residential accommodation\" as contemplated by cl."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-112400:L138:context-v4",
        "aliases": {},
        "document_id": "112400",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "(e) of the proviso to cite13†s. 14 (1) . Hence they made a joint request to remand the case to the Tribunal for a finding on the said question on the basis of the evidence already on record. Accepting this joint request, the learned Judge remanded the case to the Tribunal."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-112400:L139:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-112400:L139:span7": [
            260,
            444
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "112400",
        "stage": "PRIOR_COURT_FINDING",
        "text": "The latter, after a consideration of the materials on record as well as the extent of the premises in the occupation of the landlord and also having due regard to the number of family members living with the latter, held, in his report dated May 4, 1970, that the portion of the premises in the occupation of the landlord was not reaso- nably sufficient for a family consisting of the landlord, his wife, his son, son's wife and their children."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-112400:L140:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-112400:L140:span8": [
            42,
            138
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "112400",
        "stage": "PRIOR_COURT_FINDING",
        "text": "On this basis, he recorded a finding that the premises in the occupation of the respondent were not reasonably suitable for his residence."
      }
    ]
  },
